60,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,Option C is the most stable. It is on-site and doesn't depend on roads or external contractors.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Yumi,,Option D! It's the only one that helps the people in the outer wards who lost their buses!,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,George,,Option D is a financial trap. The running costs will bleed us dry by the second year.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,May,,Option B is just a repeat of the digitisation project from six years ago. It's a disaster waiting to happen.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,Option C... we have the volunteers for it. But who will supervise them?,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Daisuke, the tool certification is a fixed system. It's safer than managing a mobile fleet in winter.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Yumi,,"@George, how can you say it's a trap when people are literally cut off from their library?","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,George,,Because a service that shuts down after eighteen months is worse than no service at all.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,May,,"Option A is interesting. It's low-cost and relies on people, not expensive equipment or vans.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,Option A... that sounds like a lot of coordination. The staff are already so busy.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,"Option A depends on ""partner organizations."" That is another external condition we cannot control.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Yumi,,But Option A could happen in the community halls! The ones that stay open during the snow!,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,George,,"If it's in community halls, we are back to the problem of fragmented grant funding.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,May,,You're all so afraid of the world outside the building. Option A is the most human.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,I... I think Option C is the safest. It's in one place. It's... manageable.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,I stand by Option C. It is the only proposal that is truly independent of external volatility.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Yumi,,I can't vote for something that stays in the main branch. We have to reach the outer wards!,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,George,,I will vote for Option C. It is the only one that fits the endowment's capital structure.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,May,,I'll go with Option A. It's a fresh start that doesn't repeat the mistakes of the archive.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,I'll vote for C too. I don't want anyone to have to work too many extra hours.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
